WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.928
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.298 --> 00:00:07.840
SPEAKER: Give me
one minute, and I'll

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.020
show you how BeyondCorp
Enterprise can secure access

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.620
to your services from
beyond the corporate walls.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:17.050
Companies are increasingly
more distributed,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.110
as employees work
in more locations.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.830
Connecting to a VPN can be
slow for employees located

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.960
far away from the headquarters.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.860
However, granting flat access
to internal labs based only

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.900
on the network can
also be dangerous.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.300
With a network-centric
model, attackers

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.380
can exfiltrate data just by
gaining access to the network.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.380
To solve these problems,
BeyondCorp Enterprise

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.470
pushes security checks from
the network back to the user's

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.870
device and context.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:49.420
It does this by creating
a proxy in front

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.720
of apps running in GCP,
other Cloud platforms,

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:54.250
or on premises.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.070
The proxy passes through
or blocks traffic

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.790
based on the requester's device
information, their identity,

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:02.920
and hundreds of other signals.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:06.730
For example, you can choose
to allow access to HR apps

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.550
only for devices
managed by the company.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:12.460
For added security, you
can enforce multifactor

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:14.290
authentication as well.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:18.040
To secure HR apps using
Access Context Manager,

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.230
Define an access level.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.840
This level includes
requests from devices

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.900
managed by the company
and requests authenticated

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.640
with multifactor.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.400
Next, using Identity
Aware Proxy,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.820
map the new access
level to the HR web app.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.590
So next time you're
looking to shift

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:38.800
to a zero-trust,
context-diverse security model,

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.650
take a minute to look at
BeyondCorp Enterprise.

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.477
To learn more check, out
cloud.google.com/beyondcorp

00:01:44.477 --> 00:01:46.905
enterprise.

